  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A Tunisian lace shawl is a flat rectangle 180 cm long and 55 cm wide worked entirely in Tunisian crochet with a long-tail or interchangeable hook. The fabric alternates bands of solid "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "tunisian-simple-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Tunisian simple stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "openwork-panel"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "openwork panels"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of chains and single stitches that run the full length of the shawl. Blocked, the panels open into wide lace ladders."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every row has two phases. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "forward-pass"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "forward pass"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " picks up loops across the row from right to left, leaving them all on the hook. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "return-pass"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "return pass"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " then works them off from left to right until one loop remains. This is the engine of all Tunisian work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Sport weight yarn",
              "qty": "400 g",
              "substitutions": "A smooth wool-cotton blend or bamboo blend drapes well in the long rectangle format."
            },
            {
              "name": "5 mm Tunisian crochet hook (long, at least 40 cm)",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            },
            {
              "name": "Blocking mats and pins",
              "qty": "1 set"
            },
            {
              "name": "Measuring tape",
              "qty": "1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "18 Tss x 16 rows = 10 x 10 cm in sport weight with a 5 mm Tunisian hook, unblocked. Tunisian fabric does not change dramatically with blocking, but does relax slightly. Work a 25-stitch swatch across 20 rows and measure unblocked."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitch notation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "tunisian-simple-stitch"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Tss"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": Tunisian simple stitch, insert hook behind front vertical bar, pull up loop"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dc (UK): double crochet"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "forward-pass"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "FP"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": forward pass"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "return-pass"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "RP"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": return pass, ch 1, *yo, pull through 2 loops* to end"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation row"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 100. FP: insert hook into 2nd ch from hook, pull up loop. Continue pulling up 1 loop from each ch across. (100 loops on hook.) RP: ch 1, *yo, pull through 2 loops*. Repeat to end. (1 loop remains.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitch pattern: 10-stitch repeat"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The pattern repeats across 10 stitches: 6 Tss, then 1 ch-2 openwork panel (skip 2, ch 2, pick up 1 Tss), then 1 Tss to anchor. Work this repeat across all 100 foundation stitches (10 repeats of 10). Follow with RP."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On the next row, work 6 Tss over the Tss column. For the openwork section, insert the hook into the ch-2 space and pull up one loop as if it were a stitch. This is the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "openwork-panel"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "openwork panel"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " repeat that keeps the ladders aligned on every row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Working the length"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Continue working FP and RP with the 10-stitch pattern until the piece measures 180 cm. At 16 rows per 10 cm, this is approximately 288 rows. The fabric will bias slightly. This is normal for Tunisian and corrects on blocking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast off"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On the final forward pass, instead of leaving loops on the hook, work sl st into each Tss and ch-2 space across. This is the Tunisian cast-off row. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Blocking"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Soak, press out water, and pin the rectangle to 180 x 55 cm on blocking mats. The Tunisian bias flattens on blocking. The openwork panels open into full-width lace ladders only after wet blocking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Common problems",
          "intro": "Tunisian shawls have specific Tunisian-method issues.",
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Fabric biasing to one side",
              "cause": "Natural Tunisian bias from asymmetric stitch construction",
              "fix": "This is normal and corrects completely on blocking. Pin aggressively to the rectangular dimensions."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Loops falling off the hook",
              "cause": "Hook too short for the stitch count",
              "fix": "A 5 mm Tunisian hook must be at least 40 cm long for 100 stitches. Use an interchangeable Tunisian hook with an extension cable for long rows."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Openwork columns misaligned",
              "cause": "Inserting into the wrong position on the return pass",
              "fix": "The ch-2 space is a visible gap in the fabric. Insert the hook directly into the gap rather than into a vertical bar."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}